{"metadata": {"team_id": "cfda", "run_id": "gen-only_npsg13_thru0_d4c5", "run_type": "generation-only"}, "turn_id": "3-1_9", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To tape your finger after an A2 pulley injury, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Prepare Your Finger**: Ensure your finger is straight.\n2. **Apply the Tape**: Start taping from halfway between the first two creases on the front of your finger and finish halfway between the second and third creases. Overlap the tape by about 50% to provide adequate support.\n3. **Restrict Movement**: This taping method is designed to limit the ability of your finger to bend at the joint of the injured pulley, which is crucial for healing.\n4. **Buddy Taping**: Consider buddy taping your injured finger to an adjacent finger for added stability and protection.\n5. **Use Medical Tape**: If possible, use medical-grade tape, but ensure it’s not too tight to avoid cutting off circulation.\n6. **Retape as Needed**: Remember to retape your finger between climbing routes or whenever the tape feels loose, as it can stretch and lose effectiveness.\n\nThis method will help immobilize your finger and support the healing process as you gradually return to climbing.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 3.0297815799713135, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 2.9237794876098633, "clueweb22-en0006-32-19661:11": 1.998306393623352, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:2": 1.8392820358276367, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:11": 1.7468137741088867, "clueweb22-en0031-25-08597:3": 1.3567705154418945, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:11": 1.262800931930542, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:1": 1.2006518840789795, "clueweb22-en0002-05-11290:10": 1.1916496753692627, "clueweb22-en0002-05-11290:9": 1.1605185270309448, "clueweb22-en0023-44-07422:16": 1.0846302509307861, "clueweb22-en0012-34-06229:10": 1.0043623447418213, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:14": 0.9807797074317932}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am climbing regularly for the past 3 years."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-