{"metadata": {"team_id": "cfda", "run_id": "gen-only_npsg13_thru0_d4c5", "run_type": "generation-only"}, "turn_id": "3-1_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "H-taping is an effective method for supporting an A2 pulley injury. To apply H-taping, follow these steps:\n\n1. Cut a length of rigid athletic tape about 10 cm long and 1.5 cm wide, preferably using Leukoplast tape.\n2. Cut the tape in half lengthwise from both ends, leaving a 1 cm bridge in the middle.\n3. Place the tape on the injured finger with the bridge on the inside, sitting on the crease of the joint above the injured pulley.\n4. Flex your finger to 60° at the joint being taped.\n5. Wrap the upper part of the tape in a ring around the finger, then wrap another ring below the joint.\n\nThis method helps immobilize the finger joint to prevent bending and provides support during recovery. It is recommended to use H-taping for three months after a Grade 2 injury and for six months after a Grade 3 injury. Remember to retape your finger between climbs or whenever the tape starts to loosen to maintain its effectiveness.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 6.4161858558654785, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:11": 4.857207298278809, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 4.511844635009766, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 4.284430027008057, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:2": 4.187707901000977, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:7": 3.8508214950561523, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:8": 3.6885881423950195, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:5": 3.1663331985473633, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:8": 3.08768630027771, "clueweb22-en0006-32-19661:11": 2.938675880432129, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:9": 2.906651020050049, "clueweb22-en0007-15-09796:3": 2.515256404876709, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:14": 2.497121572494507}, "ptkb_provenance": []}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:12": 6.4161858558654785, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:11": 4.857207298278809, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:13": 4.511844635009766, "clueweb22-en0033-87-09727:10": 4