{"metadata": {"team_id": "cfda", "run_id": "gen-only_npsg13_thru0_d4c5", "run_type": "generation-only"}, "turn_id": "8-1_2", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To manage your feelings of overwhelm at work due to ADHD, consider implementing a few strategies tailored to your situation. Since your office is quiet, you can focus on organization and task management. Here are some effective approaches:\n\n1. **Break Tasks Down**: Divide larger projects into smaller, manageable tasks. This can make them feel less daunting and help you maintain focus.\n\n2. **Prioritize Tasks**: Use a priority matrix to identify urgent and important tasks. This can help you focus on what needs to be done first and reduce overwhelm.\n\n3. **Set Time Limits**: Allocate specific time blocks for each task. Use a timer to keep yourself accountable, which can also help you stay focused.\n\n4. **Take Regular Breaks**: Incorporate short breaks throughout your day to recharge. This can help prevent burnout and improve your overall productivity.\n\n5. **Use Organizational Tools**: Consider using digital tools or apps designed for task management, like Trello or Asana, to keep track of your responsibilities and deadlines.\n\n6. **Communicate with Your Team**: If you're feeling overwhelmed, don't hesitate to discuss your workload with your supervisor or colleagues. They may be able to help redistribute tasks or provide support.\n\n7. **Consult a Professional**: If feelings of overwhelm persist, consider speaking with a mental health professional who can provide tailored strategies and support.\n\nImplementing these strategies can help you manage your workload more effectively and reduce feelings of overwhelm associated with ADHD.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0037-47-14866:15": 0.4172891676425934, "clueweb22-en0023-37-18046:0": 0.3845788836479187, "clueweb22-en0045-11-16665:15": 0.373526006937027, "clueweb22-en0022-51-00776:5": 0.36687523126602173, "clueweb22-en0023-22-00066:6": 0.3124106526374817, "clu