{"metadata": {"team_id": "cfda", "run_id": "gen-only_npsg13_thru0_d4c5", "run_type": "generation-only"}, "turn_id": "8-1_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To manage your attention during meetings, consider implementing a few effective strategies:\n\n1. **Schedule Wisely**: Choose times for meetings when your team's energy is lower, such as Thursdays, to reserve high-energy days for more demanding tasks.\n\n2. **Plan Ahead**: Always prepare a clear agenda for each meeting and share it in advance. This helps keep the discussion focused and ensures everyone knows what to expect.\n\n3. **Limit Attendees**: Curate the list of participants to include only those essential to the meeting. This minimizes distractions and keeps conversations relevant.\n\n4. **Set Objectives**: Define clear objectives for the meeting and allocate specific times for each agenda item to maintain structure.\n\n5. **Record and Recap**: Take notes during the meeting, record decisions, and end with clear action items. Send a recap afterward to ensure everyone is on the same page.\n\n6. **Avoid Surprise Meetings**: Schedule meetings in advance to allow for better planning and to reduce disruptions to your workflow.\n\n7. **Consider Alternatives**: If the meeting's content can be conveyed through email, opt for that instead, allowing recipients to reference the information later without needing to meet.\n\nBy implementing these strategies, you can enhance your focus and productivity during meetings while managing your attention effectively.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0002-06-10108:4": 3.7964470386505127, "clueweb22-en0027-55-15986:14": 2.9765517711639404, "clueweb22-en0016-28-01007:8": 2.5807628631591797, "clueweb22-en0043-07-14902:9": 2.5440313816070557, "clueweb22-en0002-38-13953:10": 2.498525619506836, "clueweb22-en0038-46-17021:12": 2.4325528144836426, "clueweb22-en0046-28-10827:11": 2.3656511306762695, "clueweb22-en0012-33-13598:13": 2.2209863662719727, "clueweb22-en0040-35-16882:0": 2.069